From 2a5484af0a4e482f5e1152cde2d0013d520be4ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:31:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/54] ATTRIB: no keep_duplicate_records in the DWG (R2010+)

In AutoCAD's R2010, R2013 and R2018 files (ACadSharp samples
sample_AC1024/1027/1032.dwg) the data stream of an ATTRIB ends right
after the lock_position_flag, i.e. at bitsize - 17 - string data_size.
ODA 20.4.4 and ACadSharp have no further field there; only ATTDEF has
the repeated version RC (here keep_duplicate_records) before the prompt.
Reading one more RC gave "Invalid ATTRIB.keep_duplicate_records 64/65/72"
and wrote an extra byte. Kept for DXF and JSON.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dwg.spec | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dwg.spec b/src/dwg.spec
index 96b4343..31f31b4 100644
--- a/src/dwg.spec
+++ b/src/dwg.spec
@@ -376,11 +376,14 @@ DWG_ENTITY (ATTRIB)
     SINCE (R_2007a) {
       FIELD_B (lock_position_flag, 0); // 70
     }
-    // XRECORD subclass
+    // Not in the DWG: in AutoCAD's R2010, R2013 and R2018 files the data
+    // stream ends after the lock_position_flag (ODA 20.4.4, ACadSharp).
+    // Only ATTDEF has the repeated version RC (here keep_duplicate_records).
+#if !defined(IS_DECODER) && !defined(IS_ENCODER)
     SINCE (R_2010b) {
       FIELD_RC (keep_duplicate_records, 0);
-      VALUEOUTOFBOUNDS (keep_duplicate_records, 1)
     }
+#endif
   }
   COMMON_ENTITY_HANDLE_DATA;
   SINCE (R_13b1) {
-- 
